<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Frisia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ostfriesland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a> is a coastal region of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> between the Dollart and the Jade, including the East Frisian Islands. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was part of the Frisian Freedom, governed by local chieftains, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-cirksena">Cirksena</a> family united it as an imperial county in 1464. It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1744 and to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> in 1815.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-frisia.jpg" alt="East Frisia" width="320" height="294" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Onno · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ostfriesland_hervorgehoben.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
